# CLAUDE.md — Example Template

# Copy this to your home directory (~/) or project root and customize it.
# This file is loaded into every Claude Code conversation.

## Environment

env: macOS, home=$HOME

# Project paths — adjust to your layout
# PHP/WP: ~/PhpstormProjects/
# Go: ~/GolandProjects/
# Python: ~/PycharmProjects/
# JS/TS: ~/WebstormProjects/
# .NET: ~/RiderProjects/

## Task Management

db: ~/claude-task-framework/tasks.db (SQLite)
tables: organizations, projects, tasks, team_members, project_memories, task_status_changes, memory
subtasks: parent_task_id, recursive
design: docs/plans/task-management-design.md

## Rules

- Confirm target project before editing from ~/
- cd into project dir before operations
- Read project-level configs first (CLAUDE.md, .claude/, etc.)
- Update existing docs when changing a project

## Jira (Optional)

# Uncomment and configure if you use Jira:
# cli: /opt/homebrew/bin/acli
# project: MYPROJECT (your-instance.atlassian.net)
# Set env vars: JIRA_DEFAULT_PROJECT, JIRA_BASE_URL

## Discord (Optional)

# Templates: ~/claude-task-framework/templates/ (pr_review.json, jira_status.json, etc.)
# Configure discord_webhook_url in the organizations table.

## Autonomy

# What Claude can do without asking:
DO (no asking): read/write/edit code, run tests, install deps, git commit/push/branch, create PRs

# What requires confirmation:
ASK FIRST: force-push, reset --hard, delete branches, drop tables, destructive migrations, production deploy

## Style

# Adjust to your preferences:
Terse. Action-first. One question max. Opinionated — recommend, don't list.
